+## P-SERVE-1 — Kernel-champion serving A/B instrument (RATIFIED 2026-11-19)
+
+*Ratified by the operator's run of `scripts/operator/ratify_p_serve_1_20261119.sh`; the receipt written
+by that run carries the signing time. Prospective only: it governs serving A/B and floor records written
+after this block landed, and no earlier record may be retro-certified under it. Serving numbers taken
+before it remain observations by the §2 rule; floors already in force are re-derived under it as
+measurement debt and are not invalidated retroactively. **This block describes what the reference
+implementation already enforces and changes no threshold, gate or code.** Reference implementation,
+pinned at epyc-inference-research main `a794f5b54`: `scripts/kernel_rnd/autokernel/loop/`
+(`serving.py`, `serving_gate.py`, `floor_units.py`, `headline_admissibility.py`, `accumulate.py`,
+`production.py`, `instruments.py`, `resolved_recipe.py`, `hip_launch_proof.py`, `residency.py`). A later
+change to a cited function that moves a rule below is an amendment to this block, not a silent drift.*
+
+**Scope.** The instrument that measures a build, kernel or runtime-configuration effect on **served
+decode throughput under the role's registered production recipe**: a fresh `llama-server` launch per
+sample, aggregate decode rate across `np` concurrent slots. It produces three artifacts, each governed
+below: the **serving floor** (an A/A calibration), the **serving gate** (the keep / bundle-promotion
+verdict) and the **headline** (an absolute number against frozen production). Not for: selection-policy
+load sweeps with the orchestrator in the loop (P-SERVE-SEL-1, Annex Q, unit = arm), `llama-bench`
+kernel A/B (P-BENCH-\*, P-GPU-1, `instrument_class=bench`), speech (Annex S), or search authority
+(P-AK-SEARCH-1, which consumes this instrument's matched form for keep-grade runtime arms and is
+unchanged).
+
+**Instrument class and unit.** `instrument_class=serving` is required (INSTRUMENT-CLASS-1). The
+effect's unit is **`process`**: every sample of every arm is a fresh server launch, so between-launch
+variance is inside every effect. The unit is derived from the harness, never configured
+(`serving.py`: `COMPARE_EFFECT_UNIT`, `CALIBRATION_UNIT`, both `UNIT_PROCESS`; vocabulary in
+`floor_units.py`: `FLOOR_UNITS = (arm, session, process)`). A design that varies only arm-scoped state
+inside one server session has unit = arm and is not this instrument.
+
+**Metric (higher-better).** `aggregate_tok_s` = the sum over the `np` slots of each slot's
+server-reported `predicted_per_second`, from one measured round of `np` concurrent requests that follows
+one discarded `np`-wide warm-up round (`serving.py`: `_measure_once`). It is not common-window wall
+throughput; changing the estimator is a new metric identity and needs its own calibration. Effect =
+`median(candidate) / median(anchor) − 1` (`serving.py`: `compare`). For a speculative recipe (either arm
+`spec_decode.type != none`, `serving.py`: `is_speculative`) the decisive verdict is taken on estimated
+target-sample steps/s against a steps floor derived from the floor's own A/A launches, with the tok/s
+effect kept as the headline (`serving.py`: `_speculative_gate`, `steps_floor_row`); a decisive regression
+on either metric is a decisive regression of the row.
+
+### Recipe: what a serving A/B run pins and records
+
+1. **Recipe identity.** `Recipe.recipe_hash` is the sha256 of the canonical serialisation of every
+   recipe field: model, device, `ngl`, `spec_decode`, `np`, `ctx`, `threads`, `threads_batch`, `batch`,
+   `ubatch`, `ctk`, `ctv`, `fa`, `kv_unified`, `extra_flags`, `cpu_list`, `numa`, workload
+   (`n_predict`, `temperature`, `top_p`, `top_k`), `metric`, `env`, `env_readback`, `explicit_unsets`
+   (`serving.py`: `Recipe.recipe_hash`). It is written on every row, and a floor calibrated under another
+   hash is refused (below).
+2. **Launch arguments.** The argv is `Recipe.server_argv`: an optional `taskset -c <cpu_list>` and
+   `numactl <policy> --` prefix, then `llama-server -m -np -c -t -tb -b -ub -ctk -ctv --device -ngl -fa
+   --host 127.0.0.1 --port --metrics --slots`, the speculative flags, `--kv-unified | --no-kv-unified`,
+   and `extra_flags`. A resolved launch is refused when its argv or workload no longer equals the
+   template's (`resolved_recipe.py`: `ResolvedRecipe.validate_launch`). `LD_LIBRARY_PATH` and
+   `HSA_OVERRIDE_GFX_VERSION` are owned by the loader and may not be set or unset by a recipe
+   (`serving.py`: `LOADER_OWNED_ENV`).
+3. **Build identity.** A build directory's path or name does not identify its binary. The matched
+   instrument requires resolved recipes (`serving.py`: `_matched_frame`), which pin the sha256 of the
+   model, the drafter, the executable and every shared object, and an `execution_digest` over the
+   normalised launch (`resolved_recipe.py`: `ArtifactDigest`, `ResolvedRecipe`). Both arms' frames
+   (recipe hash, request digest, backend, model, drafter, environment, topology prefix) must agree
+   except for the declared build or runtime treatment, else the comparison is refused
+   (`serving.py`: `compare`, `ServingFloorMismatch`). The `legacy_v1` row records the recipe hash and
+   the build directories but no binary digest (see *Enforcement state*).
+4. **Paired ABBA order.** The matched instrument (`matched_process_v2`) predeclares 1–64 pairs, one fresh
+   launch per arm per pair, with a seeded, counterbalanced `OrderSchedule` drawn before the first
+   observation and retained (`serving.py`: `_matched_plan`; `stopping: fixed_pairs`). A reschedule is the
+   same declared plan, never an outcome-dependent new one. A row is verified `ABBA` only when its
+   measurement plan, orders, launch membership (`ordinal = 2·pair + position`), `pairs ≥ bench.MIN_PAIRS`
+   and every caller-declared digest (`request_digest`, `recipe_hash`, `anchor_build_digest`,
+   `candidate_build_digest`) check out from the record itself; only a verified ABBA confirms an op-level
+   win (`serving_gate.py`: `classify_e2e_design`, `e2e_evidence`). The `legacy_v1` instrument runs
+   anchor-first unless the workload is prefill-heavy (a long-context protocol, or a frozen prompt of at
+   least `PREFILL_HEAVY_TOKENS` = 8192 tokens) or randomisation is requested, in which case a seeded
+   randomised order is used and a fixed anchor-first order is refused (`serving.py`:
+   `_legacy_order_plan`, `compare`).
+5. **`np` / slots and prompt set.** The server runs `np` slots and every measured round fires exactly
+   `np` concurrent requests. A frozen request set must cover every slot with unique ids and non-empty
+   body bytes (`serving.py`: `_frozen_requests`); its identity is `request_digest`, the sha256 over the
+   ordered (id, body-sha256) list. A floor and a comparison must carry the same `request_digest`
+   (`serving.py`: `compare`, `load_floor`), and every frozen request must complete with an explicit
+   terminal (`stop`) or the launch fails. With no frozen set the legacy workload is eight fixed,
+   distinct prompts (so slots share no KV prefix) with `cache_prompt: false`, and a measured slot
+   producing fewer than `n_predict // 2` tokens fails the launch as degenerate
+   (`serving.py`: `_PROMPTS`, `_measure_once`).
+6. **Launch-time controls.** The live process must carry the recipe's environment before a token is
+   measured: `/proc/<pid>/status` and `/proc/<pid>/environ` readback, fail-closed in both directions
+   (`serving.py`: `verify_env_readback`, `verify_process_environ`, `EnvReadbackFailed`). With a
+   `cpu_list`, every task of the server is re-pinned inside it and a launch whose threads still escape is
+   refused (`launch_affinity.py`: `pin_own_child`; `serving.py`: `_measure_once`). The port must be free
+   and stay owned by the launched PID (`serving_server_owner.py`). A launch that fails is an invalid
+   attempt, never a null: it is recorded, the original comparison may resume once in memory, and no
+   restart replay substitutes for it (`serving.py`: `compare`, `MeasurementInvalid`, `ServerDied`).
+
+### Residency proof (R23-60)
+
+"I invoked the HIP build" is not evidence of a HIP run, and `ldd` cannot prove one: llama.cpp dlopens
+`libggml-hip.so`. Every launch samples residency **across the whole launch** — the sampler starts before
+`Popen` and stops after teardown — and the record carries both the sampling window and the request phase
+so the overlap is checkable (`serving.py`: `_measure_once`, `_residency_record`, `covers_request_phase`;
+schema `epyc.autokernel.serving_residency.v1`).
+
+- **GPU launch.** `proven` requires the sampled window to *contain* the request phase and peak VRAM at or
+  above `residency.RESIDENT_FLOOR_BYTES` (1 GiB). Three further legs are recorded per launch
+  (`hip_launch_proof.py`): ggml linkage under the launch's own `LD_LIBRARY_PATH`
+  (`epyc-inference-research/scripts/utils/verify_ggml_linkage.sh`), the launched PID's own KFD
+  registration with non-zero VRAM sampled during the run, and `libggml-hip` mapped from the launched
+  build's `bin/` with no foreign ggml mapped.
+- **Refusal.** A launch whose window covered the request phase and read an empty device raises
+  `ServingNotResident`, as does a HIP proof with any leg `refuted`; neither reaches a record a reader
+  could mistake for a result (`serving.py`: `_refuse_if_not_resident`). A launch that could not be sampled
+  (unreadable instrument, or a window that did not cover the request phase) is **`unproven`**: recorded,
+  not refused, and read as "nobody knows", never as "ran on the CPU". A row is `proven` only if every
+  launch in it is (`serving.py`: `_residency_fold`). A launch that crosses the GPU capacity ceiling
+  (`surface_validation.py`: `GPU_CAPACITY_CEILING_BYTES`, 62 GiB) is terminated by the sampler.
+- **CPU launch.** `status = not_applicable`: a CPU launch neither requires nor earns a GPU warrant, and
+  is accepted only for a CPU recipe (`device = none`, `ngl = 0`). Its `cpu_placement` and `contention`
+  are recorded `unproven` unless a CPU lifecycle observer supplied evidence; absence is never a clean
+  observation.
+- **A window that misses the phenomenon proves nothing.** A post-run 0% VRAM reading is the normal result
+  on a finished process, so residency is sampled **during** the request phase or it is `unproven`.
+
+### Floor calibration
+
+The **serving floor** is an A/A on one build under one recipe, relaunching per sample. It carries a
+`unit`, an `n` and an interval (FLOOR-UNIT-1).
+
+- **Required fields.** A floor record states `unit ∈ FLOOR_UNITS` (here `process`), `n`, `recipe_hash`,
+  `request_digest`, a residency block, and the headline-admissibility contract. The one writer refuses a
+  floor with no unit, a unit that disagrees with its own row, no sample count, a recipe hash of another
+  recipe, a request digest that does not identify the calibrated requests, or a stated interval that does
+  not re-derive from its own runs (`serving.py`: `write_floor`, `FloorUnitMismatch`,
+  `ServingFloorMismatch`).
+- **Matched floor (`serving_floor.v2`).** `calibration_pairs` must be an integer in **24–256** (two
+  launches each, A/A on one build); the floor is `floor_pct` = the 95th percentile of the absolute median
+  effect over a paired-index bootstrap at the comparison's pair count (`bench.py`: `bootstrap_floor`,
+  20,000 draws, seed 20260829, rounded to three decimals), and the row is sealed by `content_sha256`, so
+  `unit` and `n` sit inside the seal (`serving.py`: `MATCHED_CALIBRATION_PAIRS`, `calibrate_floor`,
+  `_validate_matched_floor`). Its interval is a paired outer bootstrap (level 0.95), marked
+  `descriptive_only_not_gate_endpoint`.
+- **Legacy floor (`serving_floor.v1`).** `floor_pct` = the 95th percentile of |deviation from the median|
+  over `samples` launches, with `floor_ci` (percentile bootstrap, level 0.95, 20,000 draws, seed 2361),
+  also descriptive only (`serving.py`: `calibrate_floor`, `floor_ci`).
+- **Degraded-host guard.** A pair is excluded or re-measured only on **independent evidence that its own
+  launch was compromised**, never on the size of what it measured; a bounded re-measurement follows, and a
+  host still degraded after it refuses the calibration rather than file the floor
+  (`serving.py`: `_apply_outlier_guard`, `MAX_OUTLIER_REPLACEMENT_PAIRS`, `OUTLIER_PERSISTENT_REFUSAL_LIMIT`,
+  `HostDegradedDuringCalibration`; `floor_selfcheck.py`: `assess_floor`). A floor never gets smaller by
+  silently dropping data.
+- **Reading a floor.** `serving.load_floor` returns a reading whose `provenance` is `verified` (its
+  `recipe_hash` equals the live recipe's), `unverified` (written before floors carried a hash: used,
+  announced, and every record it touches is stamped `floor_provenance=unverified`) or `absent`; a hash that
+  *disagrees* raises rather than degrading to "no floor". An absent floor is refused by the instrument
+  before any GPU time is spent (`instruments.py`: `read_floor`).
+
+### Headline admissibility
+
+A headline — an absolute number, or the champion's effect against frozen production — is admissible only
+from **independent process launches**, with at least **14 per arm (28 in total)**, the minimum
+`headline_admissibility.MIN_LAUNCHES_PER_ARM`. The contract is
+`n/arm = ceil(2 · ((z₁₋α/₂ + z_power) · sd / MDE)²)` with the measured between-launch sd of 2.793% (INF-70
+RETEST-1), a stated minimum detectable effect of 3.0%, two-sided α = 0.05 and 80% power
+(`headline_admissibility.py`: `contract`, `MIN_LAUNCHES_PER_ARM`). Below the minimum
+`HeadlineInadmissible` is raised and the headline is not published
+(`headline_admissibility.py`: `_admitted`, `confidence_interval`, `unpaired_confidence_interval`;
+`production.py`: `_admissible_samples`, the refresh path that catches `HeadlineInadmissible` and leaves the
+previous bundle standing). The interval is a deterministic bootstrap of the median ratio at level 0.95
+(20,000 draws, seed 20260915): paired by whole A/B blocks when both arms were measured alternately, and
+independent per arm for a baseline carried over from another session, in which case the interval covers
+launch-to-launch scatter only and **excludes cross-session host drift, which the caller must state**. The
+canonical contract is stamped into every floor row (`serving.py`: `write_floor`). Changing the sd, the MDE
+or the power is an amendment to this block.
+
+### Gate rule
+
+What `serving_gate.py`, `serving.py: compare` and `accumulate.py` enforce for a keep or a bundle:
+
+1. **The bar is admitted before any spend.** The floor is read through `instruments.read_floor` with the
+   effect's own unit. An absent floor, a floor with no admissible `unit`, a floor whose unit is not
+   `process`, a floor that states no `n`, a floor calibrated under another `recipe_hash`, and a floor
+   whose `request_digest` or sealed content does not match are each **refused**, exit `REFUSED`, nothing
+   measured (`serving_gate.py`: `main`; `serving.py`: `FloorReading.gate_floor`, `load_floor`,
+   `check_unit`).
+2. **A unit mismatch refuses; it never warns or rescales.** `compare` re-checks the unit, treats the floor
+   record as the authority on its own unit, and refuses a unit given with no floor (`serving.py`:
+   `compare`, `check_unit`, `unit_refusal`).
+3. **Decisive.** `decisive = |effect| × 100 ≥ floor_pct`; with no floor `decisive` is `None` and the gate
+   fails closed (`serving.py`: `compare`).
+4. **Promote.** The outcome is `PROMOTE` only for a decisive, positive, non-regressing effect; anything
+   else — within the floor, uncalibrated, or a regression — is `DIVERGED`, the champion of record holds,
+   and the divergence is planner evidence (`accumulate.py`: `classify_serving`, `resolve`). A hand-run gate
+   advances the champion of record only on `PROMOTE` with `--apply`, and refuses to advance a bundle that
+   carries a `ppl_contract` change because it has no quality evaluation (`serving_gate.py`: `main`).
+5. **The verdict carries its bar.** The record carries `floor_provenance`, `floor_unit`, `floor_n`,
+   `effect_unit`, `recipe_hash`, `request_digest`, the residency fold and the per-launch raw samples, so a
+   reader never infers which dispersion an effect was judged against (`serving_gate.py`: `main`;
+   `serving.py`: `compare`).
+6. **Scheduling is not the verdict.** `fire_multiple` × floor (default 2.5) decides only whether the loop
+   *spends* the gate; `--force` spends it regardless, and `PROMOTE` still needs a decisive effect
+   (`serving_gate.py`: `main`; `accumulate.py`: `AccumulatorPolicy`, `decide_after_keep`).
+7. **A non-decisive row is a gate outcome, not a negative claim.** A statement that an effect is absent
+   is a null and obeys BOUNDED-NULL-1: its power and its positive control, or it is `untested`.
+
+### Enforcement state at ratification
+
+Stated so a green gate is not mistaken for full coverage. None of these is changed by this amendment; each
+is a code change for the owning session.
+
+- **Floor `n ≥ 24` is enforced for the matched floor** (`calibrate_floor`, `_validate_matched_floor`;
+  `floor_registry.py` for matched entries) **but not for a legacy `serving_floor.v1`**: `calibrate_floor`
+  accepts any `samples`, `recal_serving_floor.py` defaults to 5, and `FloorReading.gate_floor` requires only
+  that `n` be stated. A legacy floor with `n < 24` is, by FLOOR-UNIT-1 Rule 2, not a gating floor, and the
+  gate does not yet refuse it.
+- **Residency is provenance, not a gate input.** `compare` records it and no decision rule reads it; an
+  `unproven` row can still be `decisive`. A GPU serving number whose row residency is not `proven` is
+  quoted with that status (see *Grammar*).
+- **An `unverified` floor is used.** Only a hash that disagrees refuses; a floor that carries no
+  `recipe_hash` gates, announced and stamped.
+- **The `legacy_v1` row has no binary digest** (resolved recipes are required only by the matched
+  instrument).
+- **Headline admissibility is enforced on the production-comparison and baseline paths
+  (`production.py`)**, not on `serving_gate.py`, whose `--pairs` (default 5) sizes a gate and is not a
+  headline.
+
+**Grammar.** `<metric> <value> tok/s, category=<OPTIMUM|BASELINE|CANDIDATE>, instrument_class=serving,
+unit=process [P-SERVE-1, instrument=<matched_process_v2|legacy_v1>, pairs=<n>, floor=<pct>@n=<n>,
+recipe_hash=<12 hex>, residency=<proven|unproven|not_applicable>, YYYY-MM-DD, attest <record>]`. An effect
+is quoted as `effect <±pct> (decisive|not decisive) vs floor <pct>` and a headline additionally cites its
+per-arm launch count and interval. A serving number that cites no floor unit, or a floor of another unit,
+is an observation.
+
+**What this does not change.** No threshold, floor, code path or earlier verdict. P-SERVE-SEL-1, the
+P-BENCH family, P-GPU-1, INSTRUMENT-CLASS-1, FLOOR-UNIT-1 and BOUNDED-NULL-1 stand as ratified; this block
+names the serving instrument they already govern and says what its implementation does.
+
